   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\n<div>Hi everyone!</div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone know how to specify non-zero means to compute a multivariate Gaussian density with TMB?</div><div>The two TMB functions that I found for this are listed \n<a href=\"https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/namespacedensity.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/namespacedensity.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461854776000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JHuhab6pH3lDmvUAX5lD4\">here</a>\n\n: <a href=\"https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/classdensity_1_1MVNORM__t.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/classdensity_1_1MVNORM__t.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461854776000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0EN74NZciKjbrPNiAtECYM\">MVNORM_t</a> (user-provided covariance matrix) and\n<a href=\"https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/classdensity_1_1UNSTRUCTURED__CORR__t.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/classdensity_1_1UNSTRUCTURED__CORR__t.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461854776000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3pkU08RnDMYVnKeXM0hsJP\">UNSTRUCTURED_CORR_t</a> (unstructured correlation matrix) but they both assume zero means<br></div><div><br></div><div>As a last resort, I can write a function to do this, but ideally someone has already done it :)<br></div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks!</div>\n\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
